ariston-remotethermo — STCA plugin
==================================

Out-of-tree plugin for `starter-configurable-adapter` that talks to the
Ariston Net / Remotethermo cloud. No on-disk state (cookies and caches
are in-process only).

1. Prerequisites
----------------

* starter-configurable-adapter (headers + library), installed or a local
  build tree
* GLib / GObject / GIO / GModule
* libxml2, json-glib
* libsoup 3.x or 2.4

2. Build (against a local adapter tree)
---------------------------------------

From this directory, with the adapter already built as a sibling under
`../../configurable-adapter` (paths relative to this plugin):

    $ ./autogen.sh
    $ ./configure --with-stca=../../configurable-adapter
    $ make

Or against an installed adapter:

    $ ./configure
    $ make
    $ sudo make install

3. Run
------

Edit `examples/ariston-remotethermo.stca.xml` (credentials), then:

    $ LD_LIBRARY_PATH=../../configurable-adapter/lib/.libs \
      ../../configurable-adapter/src/starter-configurable-adapter \
        -c examples/ariston-remotethermo.stca.xml \
        -p .libs

4. Configuration
----------------

Required XML children: `host`, `user`, `password`, `gw`.

Optional: `poll-interval` (default 60s), `metering-ttl` (2h),
`features-ttl` / `session-ttl` (12h), `force`, `verbose`.

